-- title:
--   Lifting an unramified complete DVR into an adic completion
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ and $A$ be discrete valuation rings (commutative domains with the discrete valuation ring property), with $A$ an $A_0$-algebra whose structure map $A_0 \to A$ is a local homomorphism and is injective. Let $W_0$ be a further discrete valuation ring which is complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology (in the sense of `IsAdicComplete` for $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$), equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure whose structure map is local, and assume $W_0$ is unramified over $A_0$ in the sense that $\mathfrak m_{W_0} = \mathfrak m_{A_0} W_0$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{A_0}$ under $A_0 \to W_0$, and that the residue extension $\kappa(W_0)/\kappa(A_0)$ is finite as a module and separable. Let $\chi \colon \kappa(W_0) \to \kappa(A)$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with $A_0$, meaning $\chi(\overline{a_{W_0}}) = \overline{a_A}$ for every $a \in A_0$, where $a_{W_0}$ and $a_A$ denote the images of $a$ in $W_0$ and in $A$. Write $\hat A$ for the $\mathfrak m_A$-adic completion of $A$. Then there exists a ring homomorphism $\psi \colon W_0 \to \hat A$ such that: for every $a \in A_0$, $\psi(a_{W_0})$ is the image of $a_A$ in $\hat A$; $\psi$ carries $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ into the maximal ideal of $\hat A$; and for every $w \in W_0$ there is $a \in A$ with $\overline a = \chi(\overline w)$ in $\kappa(A)$ and $\psi(w) - a \in \mathfrak m_A \hat A$, the ideal of $\hat A$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_A$. The last clause is the assertion that $\psi$ induces $\chi$ on residue fields, expressed without reference to $\kappa(\hat A)$.
--
--   This is the standard lifting property of an unramified complete discrete valuation ring with finite separable residue extension: such a $W_0$ maps to the completion of any discrete valuation ring dominating $A_0$, with the residue map prescribed. It is used in the construction of cyclotomic Drinfeld charts on modular curves, where it supplies the local homomorphism from the cyclotomic coefficient ring into the completed local ring along which the chart is pushed forward, together with the residue compatibility consumed there; the proof combines the existence of a separable primitive polynomial for $W_0$ over $A_0$ with a Hensel lift of one of its residual roots in $\hat A$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_ringHom_adicCompletion_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_residueField.lean

